From: Max Pain (maxpain) via FRRouting/frr#23480
Subject: [PATCH] zebra: read kernel route notifications in order with link
 events

Backport of https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/pull/23480 (head 651685cb94)
to FRR 10.7.1, zebra changes only. Upstream fixed the same race in master
with #23356 ("Final conversion to dplane", merged 2026-10-11), which is not
in any 10.x release.

zebra read kernel route and nexthop notifications on the main pthread's
netlink socket and link/address notifications on the dplane pthread's
socket, so nothing kept them in the kernel's order. A route added to a VRF
table right after the VRF device was created (ovn-controller route exchange
does exactly that) could be handled before the VRF: it was filed under the
default VRF, never redistributed into the VRF's BGP instance, and a later
kernel delete did not match it (FRRouting/frr#18041).

Route and nexthop notifications are now read on the dplane socket too and
queued to the main pthread in order with the interface events. Conflicts
with 10.7.1 resolved by keeping 10.7.1's kernel_init() and only moving the
route and nexthop groups to the dplane socket, and by adding only
DPLANE_OP_KERNEL_NOTIFY to enum dplane_op_e.

